0335-negroni-bt-power-follows-client: Bluetooth on/off from Settings (owner bug 2026-10-27: "if I turn on Bluetooth
I can't turn it off").

Observed [V logs/usblog-20261026-233816.txt, kernel without 0334]: stage A stops at step 4, the transport says
"not usable (sends fail with EIO)", bluetoothd connects with "chip FAILED" and then logs nothing more in the kernel
log and does not crash: its power-on never ends, so the switch cannot go off. (The ~2 min repeats 02:02:43, 02:04:39,
02:06:35 are whole phone reboots: "phone interface gone" lines, launchd pid 1 boot-args again, bluetoothd pid 85.)

1. Dead chip (stage A or HCI stage failed): every host command gets a local Command Complete, status 0x03
   (Hardware Failure), instead of EIO; other packets are dropped. negronibt_dead=0 = EIO as before,
   negronibt_dead=2 = refuse the client (ECONNREFUSED / ENXIO).
2. Working chip: power follows the client. The last client closing starts a timer (negronibt_off_ms, 3000);
   then a power worker drives BT_EN low (negroni_bt_chip_off; rails and QUP2 clocks stay). The next client powers
   the chip on: line to 115200, BT_EN sequence, step 8, the whole HCI stage (negroni_bt_chip_on); its sends wait
   (negronibt_wait_ms). A failed power-on switches to the dead-chip answers. negronibt_pwrfollow=0 = always on.
   The RX thread does not read the UART while the chip is off or being powered.

Review fixes (Opus review 2026-10-27, REJECT -> fixed):
- A1: the RX thread (the only path from the queue to the kernel control socket, deliver_ctl) now also starts in
  negroni_bt_h4_fail() for the dead-chip mode; it does not read the UART while the chip is failed, off or powering.
- A2: want_on = client && off && !failed && !powering; a success clears failed; a failed runtime power-on keeps
  off and failed, and the next connect clears failed and tries once more (no back-to-back retries).
- A3: the partial RX frame (t.rxn) is dropped after each chip off/on (rx_reset flag, read by the RX thread).
- A4: dead-chip answers use a Command Status event (04 0f 04 03 01 <op>) for the commands that get Command Status
  (0x0401 Inquiry, 0x0405, 0x0406, 0x0408, 0x0409, 0x040a, 0x040f, 0x0411, 0x0413, 0x0415, 0x0417, 0x0419,
  0x041b-0x041d, 0x041f, 0x0428, 0x0429, 0x043d, 0x043e, 0x0801, 0x0803, 0x0804, 0x0807, 0x080b, 0x200d, 0x2013,
  0x2016, 0x2019, 0x2025, 0x2026, 0x2032, 0x2043, 0x205d), Command Complete for all others.

